  "script": "How's Angel Reese become the Wilt Chamberlain of the WNBA? She recently set just a WNBA single-season record of 29 double-doubles. And Atlanta still has four games left. Keep in mind the WNBA only has 44 regular season games. She has played 40 games this season, which means Reese is basically getting a double-double in three out of every four games she plays. To put that into the perspective of NBA terms over an 82-game season, that would be about 63 double-doubles. That's a pretty huge number when you consider the fact that Domantas Sabonis had 77 double-doubles in the 82-game season setting the record in the three-point era. But Wilt Chamberlain has an even crazier record in the 1966-67 season where he recorded 81 double-doubles out of a possible 81 games. So Reese isn't quite Wilt Chamberlain level yet in terms of sheer volume, but in regards to dominance over the WNBA competition around her, she is entering uncharted territory with all the records that she is breaking this season. And for anyone mentions it, she does have a field goal percentage of roughly 39% inside the paint range. And even in the NBA, if you were to catch your own misses, that would still count as an offensive rebound. So either way, this is an impressive feat.",
